<title>FRANCE: U.S. top country of origin for Paris in Dec 96.</title>
<headline>U.S. top country of origin for Paris in Dec 96.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States was the principal country of origin for import traffic handled at the Paris airports in December 1996 , Paris airport authority, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The 20 leading countries of origin for ADP imports in December 1996, with percentage change on December 1995, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  United States	 13,256 tonnes   up     8.8pct</p>
<p> 2  Canada		   2,169 tonnes   down  21.0</p>
<p> 3  Japan		    2,146 tonnes   up    21.5</p>
<p> 4  United Kingdom	 1,937 tonnes   up   102.1</p>
<p> 5  India		    1,830 tonnes   down   8.6</p>
<p> 6  Hong Kong		1,646 tonnes   up     3.8</p>
<p> 7  Germany		  1,467 tonnes   up    40.0</p>
<p> 8  Thailand		 1,274 tonnes   up    41.9</p>
<p> 9  Italy		    1,063 tonnes   up    20.3</p>
<p> 10 Senegal		    904 tonnes   up    71.7</p>
<p> 11 Kenya			884 tonnes   down   2.1</p>
<p> 12 Singapore		  855 tonnes   up    94.6</p>
<p> 13 Egypt			762 tonnes   up    72.5</p>
<p> 14 South Africa	     718 tonnes   down   0.3</p>
<p> 15 Korea			668 tonnes   up    48.1</p>
<p> 16 Brazil		     661 tonnes   up    23.0</p>
<p> 17 French West Indies     646 tonnes   down   4.2</p>
<p> 18 Morocco		    646 tonnes   down  28.4</p>
<p> 19 China			625 tonnes   down   0.2</p>
<p> 20 Switzerland		621 tonnes   up    49.0</p>
<p> Total top 20 origins   34,778 tonnes</p>
<p> Total all origins	48,320 tonnes   up    10.0</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
</text>
